<pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I2df5cbc95b8a43451cc90a17d328dde1b16b3fb4" commit="ff5101ad85ff05f265dcc332ccd9634037bac9c3" commit_message="Define ARC opt-in string markers for other modules to reference.  BUG=b:29154686 TEST=test_that &lt;IP_OF_DUT&gt; cheets_PlayStoreOptIn  Change-Id: I2df5cbc95b8a43451cc90a17d328dde1b16b3fb4 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394510 Commit-Ready: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; Tested-by: Ben Cheng &lt;bccheng@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Chung-yih Wang &lt;cywang@google.com&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394510" owner_email="bccheng@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/third_party/autotest" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/autotest" ref="refs/changes/10/394510/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Ieab3d199c7f3917d0e05df5ea80889ff8db9d84e" commit="ee50671e19c2a3761c553ca29481c255a9ce7a2e" commit_message="devtools: vimrc: envrionment for developers  Initial commit for devtools/vim, which is a directory that collects useful vim plugins for ChromeOS factory developers. When developing factory code, most of our developers would modify their own vimrc to make VIM more helpful.  For example, setup PYTHONPATH to allow autocomplete, setup pylint args to check coding styles, etc...  This CL provides some useful scripts that are shared between developers, so we don't need to maintain / implement our own version, and don't need to add project specific configurations into personal vimrc.  CQ-DEPEND=CL:394447 BUG=None TEST=manual  Change-Id: Ieab3d199c7f3917d0e05df5ea80889ff8db9d84e Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/393526 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="393526" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="11" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/26/393526/11" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1b78ad65c5e75102724d96831ee645f35f450a87" commit="358ef31f4e4baf840ab3d3d9eb1cf0269827d4b4" commit_message="devtools: vimrc: traditional to simplified conversion  Since most of our OEM, ODM's factories are in China, operators read simplified Chinese.  However, for developers in Taiwan, we type in traditional Chinese, we need to convert the typed traditional Chinese strings into simplified Chinese strings.  Use iconv(1) to convert from traditional chinese to simplified chinese.  BUG=None TEST=manual  Change-Id: I1b78ad65c5e75102724d96831ee645f35f450a87 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394466 Commit-Ready: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Wei-Han Chen &lt;stimim@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Hung-Te Lin &lt;hungte@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394466" owner_email="stimim@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="8" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/66/394466/8" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iebb7be897ed931d943233cf163bb61933b81eeb3" commit="c776ae0b5a696aab248700ac26d194043f28506c" commit_message="CRAS: alsa_jack - Use different timeout for different type of jacks.  GPIO jack on some boards need long timeout for working correctly. However that affects HCTL jacks on some boards to wait too long. Use different timeout for each of them so both work happily.  BUG=chromium:624819 TEST=Verified on big that HDMI node got selected soon after plugged in.  Change-Id: Iebb7be897ed931d943233cf163bb61933b81eeb3 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/39446