ld/reef/opt/google/cr50/firmware/cr50.bin  Change-Id: Ib7f372b4ed2fa711f6df1d7886db473ca04cc8ac Signed-off-by: Vadim Bendebury &lt;vbendeb@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394307 Reviewed-by: Furquan Shaikh &lt;furquan@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394307" owner_email="vbendeb@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="2" project="chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/chromiumos-overlay" ref="refs/changes/07/394307/2" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I1489165dc134e058059b16b7346bffa0c135815f" commit="8448cfa33dcab200990ccce21aee489d7ad2e76e" commit_message="CRAS: hfp - Use dummy timestamp for last buffer change  HFP device should use dummy timestamp for last buffer change, that is, use current time. HFP device does not consume or capture samples steadily, so it might happen that the timestamp for last buffer change was a long time ago, and it breaks how timestamp mechanism works for setting audio thread wake up time for device. The result is a busy waking loop in audio thread. We should use dummy timestamp like A2DP to avoid such problem.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57175 TEST=Use HSP on the board of interest in the issue.  Signed-off-by: Cheng-Yi Chiang &lt;cychiang@chromium.org&gt; Change-Id: I1489165dc134e058059b16b7346bffa0c135815f Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394469 Tested-by: Stephen Barber &lt;smbarber@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: John Muir &lt;muirj@google.com&gt; Reviewed-by: Dylan Reid &lt;dgreid@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="0" gerrit_number="394469" owner_email="cychiang@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/adhd" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/adhd" ref="refs/changes/69/394469/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="0"/><pending_commit branch="chromeos-4.4" change_id="I9dc47f8a501743559c08c8274c993e1c395d33db" commit="68e84153ca20b8c7dd3460da917981bde3b198b0" commit_message="UPSTREAM: drm: Drop dev-&gt;event_lock spinlock around faulting copy_to_user()  In  commit cdd1cf799bd24ac0a4184549601ae302267301c5 Author: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Date:   Thu Dec 4 21:03:25 2014 +0000      drm: Make drm_read() more robust against multithreaded races  I fixed the races by serialising the use of the event by extending the dev-&gt;event_lock. However, as Thomas pointed out, the copy_to_user() may fault (even the __copy_to_user_inatomic() variant used here) and calling into the driver backend with the spinlock held is bad news. Therefore we have to drop the spinlock before the copy, but that exposes us to the old race whereby a second reader could see an out-of-order event (as the first reader may claim the first request but fail to copy it back to userspace and so on returning it to the event list it will be behind the current event being copied by the second reader).  BUG=chromium:652865 TEST=build and run kernel 4.4 on kevin  Reported-by: Thomas Hellstrom &lt;thellstrom@vmware.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Chris Wilson &lt;chris@chris-wilson.co.uk&gt; Cc: Thomas Hellstrom &lt;thellstrom@vmware.com&gt; Cc: Takashi Iwai &lt;tiwai@suse.de&gt; Cc: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; Link: http://patchwork.freedesktop.org/patch/msgid/1448462343-2072-1-git-send-email-chris@chris-wilson.co.uk Reviewed-by: Thomas Hellstrom &lt;thellstrom@vmware.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Daniel Vetter &lt;daniel.vetter@ffwll.ch&gt; (cherry picked from commit 83eb64c85b80959549c114365016276f318afeb2)  Change-Id: I9dc47f8a501743559c08c8274c993e1c395d33db Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/393346 Commit-Ready: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Dominik Behr &lt;dbehr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Stéphane Marchesin &lt;marcheu@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="393346" owner_email="dbehr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="1" project="chromiumos/third_party/kernel" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/third_party/kernel" ref="refs/changes/46/393346/1" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="Iff3ce7c48bdea6c11179fb1f401fd1feb3024c77" commit="698f587fd09c8f665441a0a7cfc8a6b05b3d16a5" commit_message="kevin: override *_CPU_GOVERNOR in laptop-mode cpufreq.conf  We need to override those macros to let laptop-mode-tools set the cpufreq governor.  BUG=chrome-os-partner:57428 TEST=verify that cpufreq governors on little and big     clusters are set to interactive after booting up  Change-Id: Iff3ce7c48bdea6c11179fb1f401fd1feb3024c77 Signed-off-by: Jeffy Chen &lt;jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com&gt; Signed-off-by: Caesar Wang &lt;wxt@rock-chips.com&gt; Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394367 Reviewed-by: Ravi Chandra Sadineni &lt;ravisadineni@chromium.org&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="394367" owner_email="jeffy.chen@rock-chips.com" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/overlays/board-overlays" ref="refs/changes/67/394367/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><pending_commit branch="master" change_id="I330e2d84751915bd0336eb069e4bde7ee932d1d9" commit="c30c1d78deb5acbef6d8ebd6e3ab5897e080f942" commit_message="dome: add Makefile for linting  For the back-end (python), we can use the same way to lint as other files in the factory repo would normally do. We'll simply delegate the linting task to factory repo's Makefile.  But for the front-end, we can't take the same approach since we're using React.  BUG=None TEST=Manually tested  Change-Id: I330e2d84751915bd0336eb069e4bde7ee932d1d9 Reviewed-on: https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/394387 Commit-Ready: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Tested-by: Mao Huang &lt;littlecvr@chromium.org&gt; Reviewed-by: Youcheng Syu &lt;youcheng@google.com&gt; " fail_count="1" gerrit_number="394387" owner_email="littlecvr@chromium.org" pass_count="0" patch_number="3" project="chromiumos/platform/factory" project_url="https://chromium-review.googlesource.com/chromiumos/platform/factory" ref="refs/changes/87/394387/3" remote="cros" total_fail_count="1"/><lkgm version="8871.0.0-rc1"/></manifest>